{
  "paraId": "480C9F2B",
  "style": "",
  "text": "In this trial, radiotherapy was administered during ICI maintenance after chemoimmunotherapy. Platinum-based chemoimmunotherapy achieves maximal tumor response in the induction phase but carries substantial toxicity. Thus, most novel ICI combinations are increasingly investigated in the maintenance setting 38–40. Our sequential design was rationally constructed to avoid additive toxicity from concurrent chemo-immunoradiotherapy and minimize target volumes by delivering focal radiotherapy in the setting of reduced tumor burden. This optimized treatment sequence appears to account for both the promising survival efficacy and the favorable safety outcomes. A relevant comparison is provided by the phase 3 KEYLYNK-006 trial, in which Gray and colleagues compared pembrolizumab plus olaparib with pembrolizumab plus pemetrexed as maintenance therapy after first-line chemoimmunotherapy in metastatic nonsquamous NSCLC: among 672 randomized patients (median follow-up 39.9 months), median progression-free survival was 7.1 months (95% CI 5.6–8.7) with olaparib versus 8.3 months (95% CI 6.9–11.5) with pemetrexed, indicating that changing the systemic maintenance partner of an ICI alone did not improve progression-free survival, in contrast to the 1-year PFS rate of 54.2% observed here when focal radiotherapy was added to ICI maintenance 38."
}

