{
  "paraId": "7B1F1599",
  "style": "",
  "text": "Non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) comprises heterogeneous pathological subtypes and molecular profiles . From a molecular and therapeutic perspective, NSCLC can be broadly categorized into 2 groups: driver gene-positive and driver gene-negative. While immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) have provided substantial clinical benefit to patients with driver gene-negative tumors, a substantial proportion of those with advanced disease still do not achieve long-term survival 1–3. Therefore, overcoming immune resistance remains a major therapeutic challenge."
}

